### Basic structure as it exists today

Currently we create an event log of every action that changes the world in an sqlite database, with plans to migrate to Postgres. This log allows for us to both undo actions and replay the entire log (currently unbuilt & unplanned, but a replay feature could plausibly be built). Currently, there is no native branching or merging; branching could be done feasibly in a database like Postgres using snapshots or cloning the database, but it will balloon quickly, and get messy. There is no native way to perform merges or to look for merge conflicts.

